Thanks for taking care of this one! I went through it against the final state of the feature (symfony/symfony#65862 plus the follow-up symfony/symfony#65871, which is the one that made the argument nullable and deprecated leaving it unset) and everything checks out: the `false`-in-8.2 / `true`-in-9.0 default, the rejection of tokens with no `typ` header at all, the case-insensitive comparison, and the note about the tokens generated by `security:oidc:generate-token`.

Two small things:

- RFC 9068 calls this "cross-JWT confusion" (§5, pointing to §2.8 of RFC 8725) rather than "token substitution" — §2.1 phrases the risk as "preventing OpenID Connect ID Tokens from being accepted as access tokens".
- "The header is read from the signed token" could spell out that only the inner JWS header is checked, not the outer JWE one.

Nothing blocking on my side.
